  "description": "Which image a name in a module's file is (ADR common-images-and-themes, decision 3). Read by both pack builders (ImageNamesTest in plugin/pack, imageNames.test.ts in the editor) and by the plugin's lookup (ImageRefConformanceTest in plugin/core). `modules` are in Project order; each one's fonts are read before its images. `ids`: the pack id of each module's image, the bare name for the first module that holds one, `<folder>:<name>` after; the theme `artisan` and a module named `kit` keep bare names, their `<folder>:` naming the common images. `cases`: a name written in a file of the module `from` (null: no module) and the id it reaches, computed from the set of ids alone, so the game finds from the pack's asset index what the builder wrote: the module's own image, another module's, else the common image of that name, whose id in the pack is `kit:<name>` (`artisan:<name>` names it whatever the module holds; `kit:<name>` is the former spelling). `also` adds the ids the index holds beyond the modules': the common images a menu asked for. Known limit of this step: the index does not say who holds a bare id, so `<module>:<name>` for an image that module does not hold falls on the bare name, then on the common image.",
